  "publicationDraft": "Tony flipped Kamara and Davis immediately after their Week 5 explosions, acquiring Brown and Robinson. Evans filled two starting slots, while Tony secured a weekly receiver. Robinson's role evaporated after his NFL move to New York, and Tony cut him December 7. Brown produced 23.60 against Evans in December, but Evans still won by 9.06. The deal delivered useful production to both sides; Tony concentrated it in one receiver while Evans spread it across two positions. Brown's consistency mattered more than Robinson's disappearing act. This was a sensible consolidation, not a guaranteed ticket to a title.",
